    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about" id="about" data-path="~/about">
  <div class="wrap about-grid">
    <figure class="portrait">
      <img src={base + "assets/simon-portrait.jpg"} width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" alt="Simon Teague, smiling, in a sage green knit polo against a pale grey background.">
      <figcaption><span>simon-portrait.jpg</span><span>utsa · class of 2029</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pr" aria-hidden="true">›</span> cat about.md</p>
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p class="serif-lead">I'm Simon. I study computer science at the University of Texas at San Antonio, class of 2029, and I spend most of my free time making tools.</p>
      <p>I like software that is small, finished and local: no accounts, no API keys where I can avoid them, and a key binding for everything. Most of what I make starts as something I wanted for myself or my friends, like a trip board that works on a train or a way to see which agent skills I had installed.</p>

      <h3>How the work gets made</h3>
      <p>Almost everything on this page was built with AI coding agents, and I'd rather say so than have you guess. My part is deciding what to build, writing the requirements and specs, breaking them into issues, running agents in separate git worktrees, integrating the results through pull requests and CI, and getting the thing released. I did not type every line and I won't claim I did.</p>

      <h3>Rowdy Creators</h3>
      <p>I'm a Project Advisor for web development and Python at Rowdy Creators, part of ACM at UTSA. On MiniMap I led the weekly standups and pull-request reviews, wrote 34 issues and coordinated 38 closed pull requests. This semester I lead the Virtual Record Store sessions, which teach HTTP, FastAPI basics and the branch, commit, pull request, review loop. I split its MVP into 22 beginner-sized issues. Those are authored, not completed.</p>
      <p>I also wrote the club's <a href="https://simonteague6.github.io/rc-setup-guide/" rel="noopener">setup guide</a> and a <a href="https://simonteague6.github.io/rc-setup-guide/first-pr.html" rel="noopener">first pull request walkthrough</a> for new members.</p>

      <h3>Home lab</h3>
      <p>A repurposed HP Z640 workstation running Ubuntu in my house: 30 containers across 14 Compose projects when I last counted, in late October 2026, on a three-disk RAID 5 array. It is one machine, not a cluster, and RAID is not a backup.</p>

      <h3>Toolbox</h3>
      <dl class="toolbox">
        <div><dt>languages</dt><dd>Python, Go, Java, JavaScript, C, Bash. TypeScript in the AI-assisted projects.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>frameworks</dt><dd>Flask, FastAPI, NetworkX, Astro. React on one team project.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>tools</dt><dd>Git, GitHub Actions, Docker and Compose, Linux, AWS, Cloudflare, Node.js, pnpm, Release Please, uv, just</dd></div>
        <div><dt>daily</dt><dd>Ghostty, Neovim with gruvbox, JetBrains Mono, lazygit</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

